; A c-style enum reaches two inline dispatch frames here. `choice_holder` is a DATA type-choice
; arm, while `gc_holder` is its array group-choice sibling. Both need the enum's early successful
; probe (`Ok(()) => return Ok(FixedEnum::I0)`) contained in the caller's variant-probe closure;
; splicing it into an ordinary deserializer would return the enum where the enclosing holder is
; required. The corpus's all-profile snapshots and compile floor, including both
; `--annotate-fields=false` flavors, keep the two call sites live.
fixed_enum = 0 / 1 / 2
choice_holder = fixed_enum / bytes
gc_holder = [ a: fixed_enum // b: tstr ]
